WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.896
They have introduced a worm
into the government system.

2
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:06.456
It's looking for something.
But what. exactly? We don't know!

3
00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:08.456
Vadim? Saara says you have something.

4
00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:09.656
A long alphanumeric.

5
00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:11.016
Possibly a ciphertext.

6
00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:12.376
Can we have it?

7
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.656
It could be really important to us.
When I'm safe.

8
00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:16.496
We need Vadim Trusov.

9
00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:18.336
We've got an attack
coming out of China at present.

10
00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:19.816
and he holds the key.

11
00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:21.856
The MAC address was stolen
on your login.

12
00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:22.896
It can't be.

13
00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:25.016
Barbara Napier.
I left her at the terminal.

14
00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:27.136
Wait. you want me
to do something for you?

15
00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:29.016
Are you out of your mind?
No. no. no.

16
00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:32.376
These are very serious allegations
you're making here. Phil.

17
00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:36.416
about a senior
and widely respected colleague.

18
00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:38.496
I'm not making allegations.

19
00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:40.496
Sorry. just too much Chinese slang.

20
00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:42.280
Calvin is all over it.

21
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:50.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

22
00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:53.160
Charlie. You OK?

23
00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:56.616
I need to ask you
a couple of questions.

24
00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:57.936
Fine. Um...

25
00:01:57.960 --> 00:01:59.096
How about later this morning?

26
00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:01.256
I've got a team briefing
first thing.

27
00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:03.656
I'm afraid it needs to be now.

28
00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:05.176
Of course.

29
00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:06.440
What's going on?

30
00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:10.136
Let's talk in private.

31
00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:11.240
Sure.

32
00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:22.936
REPORTER: Britain is at a standstill.
All UK flights are grounded.

33
00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:26.480
Banking systems are down.
and the FTSE 100 has hit a new low.

34
00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:34.040
KNOCKING

35
00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:36.680
Come in.

36
00:02:37.960 --> 00:02:40.600
Cabinet Secretary's on the phone.
Thank you.

37
00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:46.480
PHONE RINGS

38
00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:49.736
Cabinet Secretary.
how can I help you?

39
00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:51.416
Trade and Immigration
are still down.

40
00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:53.536
It's a disaster
and you pulled the plug.

41
00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:55.616
Get us back online now!

42
00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:56.640
HE SIGHS

43
00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:04.976
Well. it's been
a while since I've been in here.

44
00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:06.320
Had a refurb?

45
00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:17.896
So what's this about?

46
00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:19.816
I'm sorry. this feels strange.

47
00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:21.000
What is it?

48
00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:31.680
Could you read this statement
from Phil Draper. Malware?

49
00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:38.280
SHE CLEARS HER THROAT

50
00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:49.160
Do you remember this?

51
00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:53.440
October 2022.

52
00:03:54.680 --> 00:03:57.200
Yeah. it was a CCP malware attack.
I remember.

53
00:03:58.680 --> 00:04:00.920
What did you do at Phil's terminal?

54
00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:03.656
What did I do?

55
00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:05.336
Not very much. actually.

56
00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:07.656
You sat there for ten minutes
and didn't do much?

57
00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:09.856
Sorry. should I have done something?

58
00:04:09.880 --> 00:04:11.520
Charlie. what is going on?

59
00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:15.600
Did you access the MAC address
at Phil's terminal?

60
00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:19.320
Charlie.
why on earth would I do that?

61
00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:24.136
You were there for ten minutes.

62
00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:27.280
Someone accessed
the MAC address in that time.

63
00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:29.760
Was it you?

64
00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:32.360
Of course it wasn't me.

65
00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:36.880
Barbara. please...

66
00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:39.520
this is difficult.

67
00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:44.136
SHE SIGHS

68
00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:46.736
The Chinese was slang.

69
00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:48.016
I couldn't translate it.

70
00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:50.776
I needed someone
with better demotic proficiency

71
00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:53.376
so I brought another linguist down
to do the job.

72
00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:54.520
Who was it?

73
00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:00.656
Calvin is a friend and a colleague.
I...

74
00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:03.256
No. I'm not going to
throw him under the bus.

75
00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:05.160
His family in China got into trouble.

76
00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:08.576
We helped them out.

77
00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:09.800
He's happy to help us.

78
00:05:10.920 --> 00:05:13.080
And afterwards? What happens then?

79
00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:16.520
Then we'll take care of him.

80
00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:21.160
Calvin Song.

81
00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:28.360
Wait here.

82
00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:30.600
Joanna.

83
00:05:37.640 --> 00:05:38.920
DOOR CLOSES

84
00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:07.336
You need some rest.

85
00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:08.856
I'll work through it.

86
00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:10.296
What have we got?

87
00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:11.680
Take a look.

88
00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:16.776
We've analysed the worm.

89
00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:19.816
It's built to evade whatever
anti-malware we throw at it.

90
00:06:19.840 --> 00:06:21.816
Trade and Immigration
are still offline.

91
00:06:21.840 --> 00:06:24.936
It's contained there for the moment.
but if it breaks out...

92
00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:27.656
Home Office. NCA. MOD...

93
00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:29.736
And through us
into the American systems.

94
00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:32.280
We cannot afford
to piss off the Americans again.

95
00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:37.336
We need something heavy-duty.

96
00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:39.296
Lieutenant Williams?

97
00:06:39.320 --> 00:06:42.256
Ma'am? You remember. against ISIS?

98
00:06:42.280 --> 00:06:43.320
Tar pits.

99
00:06:44.520 --> 00:06:46.816
It's a virtual deception network

100
00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:49.536
that mimics the systems
a malware is targeting.

101
00:06:49.560 --> 00:06:52.416
The worm jumps inside
and then we trap it.

102
00:06:52.440 --> 00:06:54.160
Well. I'm feeling better already.
Let's go.

103
00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:05.000
DOOR OPENS

104
00:07:06.920 --> 00:07:08.880
Charlie.
what the hell is going on here?

105
00:07:10.520 --> 00:07:12.520
HE SIGHS You're free to go.

106
00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:14.960
Right.

107
00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:17.200
Thank you.

108
00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:23.376
I'm sorry you had
to go through all of that.

109
00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:24.456
It's fine.

110
00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:27.136
Does that mean that Calvin
accessed the MAC address?

111
00:07:27.160 --> 00:07:29.160
RADIO CHATTER

112
00:07:58.120 --> 00:08:00.736
PHONE CHIMES

113
00:08:00.760 --> 00:08:02.336
It's from Saara.

114
00:08:02.360 --> 00:08:04.776
I gave her
the new burner phone number.

115
00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:07.440
Aw. you keep your girlfriend
up-to-date.

116
00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:12.016
She says to stay where I am.

117
00:08:12.040 --> 00:08:14.136
When the trade talks in London
are concluded.

118
00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:17.696
they will send an embassy car from
Hong Kong to meet me downstairs.

119
00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:19.496
They will provide me
with a diplomatic visa

120
00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:21.616
and I will be taken
directly to the airport.

121
00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:22.840
Sounds easy-peasy.

122
00:08:24.200 --> 00:08:26.216
When do these talks finish?

123
00:08:26.240 --> 00:08:29.256
Um. she says it could be days.

124
00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:31.256
You tell your girlfriend

125
00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:33.296
she doesn't get her code unless I...

126
00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:35.136
You'll get your Bitcoin.

127
00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:36.616
And she's not my girlfriend.

128
00:08:36.640 --> 00:08:37.656
Mm.

129
00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:39.840
And be careful with this thing. Oh.

130
00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:47.520
MUSIC: Miss The Girl
by The Creatures.

131
00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:02.256
OK. so what now?

132
00:09:02.280 --> 00:09:05.040
We wait for these trade talks
to end.

133
00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:08.616
HE PUFFS

134
00:09:08.640 --> 00:09:10.880
Many people
who lose their social credit...

135
00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:17.336
they must wait in their flats
like prisoners for years.

136
00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:18.520
What do they do?

137
00:09:19.920 --> 00:09:22.480
"Use their inner resources."

138
00:09:23.800 --> 00:09:25.520
That's what my mother would say.

139
00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:28.280
I'm not sure I have any.

140
00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:30.400
I'm sure you do.

141
00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:32.880
Let me check.

142
00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:35.600
Is it here?

143
00:09:37.040 --> 00:09:39.440
Or how about here?

144
00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:44.680
Or how about...

145
00:09:45.920 --> 00:09:46.920
here?

146
00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:09.680
You're enjoying this. aren't you?

147
00:10:11.160 --> 00:10:12.160
Phil!

148
00:10:16.200 --> 00:10:18.120
It was nothing - family emergency.

149
00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:22.840
Welcome back. Thanks.

150
00:10:27.400 --> 00:10:29.496
Glad you're back. Join Max's team.

151
00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:31.016
He'll update you. OK?

152
00:10:31.040 --> 00:10:32.496
MAX: Everything all right?

153
00:10:32.520 --> 00:10:33.856
WHISPERS: Message from Charlie -

154
00:10:33.880 --> 00:10:35.976
he thinks you should go
and see Barbara.

155
00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:39.400
Shit. It's adaptive.
What anti-malware have you tried?

156
00:10:56.760 --> 00:10:58.920
DOOR OPENS

157
00:11:03.160 --> 00:11:04.320
There you are.

158
00:11:09.280 --> 00:11:11.000
I've been looking all over for you.

159
00:11:16.760 --> 00:11:18.200
So. um...

160
00:11:19.320 --> 00:11:21.016
Calvin...

161
00:11:21.040 --> 00:11:22.800
Yeah. I heard.

162
00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:29.440
I'm sorry.

163
00:11:36.720 --> 00:11:38.320
Are you OK?

164
00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:45.120
I mean. there's just...

165
00:11:46.680 --> 00:11:48.176
There's just so much to deal with.

166
00:11:48.200 --> 00:11:49.200
There's...

167
00:11:50.240 --> 00:11:51.416
the damage assessment.

168
00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:53.400
and with the trade talks.
it's just...

169
00:11:57.240 --> 00:11:58.560
It's just a mess.

170
00:12:09.920 --> 00:12:11.936
Is there...

171
00:12:11.960 --> 00:12:13.960
anything that you want to...

172
00:12:15.680 --> 00:12:16.760
talk about?

173
00:12:25.320 --> 00:12:26.720
No. I don't think so.

174
00:12:40.000 --> 00:12:42.320
I... I wanted to. um...

175
00:12:50.400 --> 00:12:51.480
What?

176
00:12:52.960 --> 00:12:54.816
Oh. damn it.

177
00:12:54.840 --> 00:12:58.496
I'm gonna have to go - I've got
a call with the Foreign Secretary.

178
00:12:58.520 --> 00:13:01.640
I'll. er...
I'll see you later. OK. OK?

179
00:13:04.720 --> 00:13:05.920
OK. OK.

180
00:13:15.320 --> 00:13:16.936
Sorry to keep you. Foreign Minister.

181
00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:20.096
Had a bit of a domestic emergency.

182
00:13:20.120 --> 00:13:22.816
I think you'll find we've got
a bit of national emergency.

183
00:13:22.840 --> 00:13:25.616
Which is why I had to close down
the systems at Trade and Immigration.

184
00:13:25.640 --> 00:13:27.376
Yeah. unfortunately
just as the Prime Minister

185
00:13:27.400 --> 00:13:30.016
is entering the final round of talks
at Admiralty.

186
00:13:30.040 --> 00:13:32.496
Yeah. with the very state players
that are attacking us.

187
00:13:32.520 --> 00:13:34.736
If this thing
gets into the NHS alone.

188
00:13:34.760 --> 00:13:37.416
life support. dialysis -
they'll all go dark.

189
00:13:37.440 --> 00:13:38.616
People will die.

190
00:13:38.640 --> 00:13:40.880
Is signing this trade deal today
THAT important?

191
00:13:42.560 --> 00:13:44.896
This is why I wanted to have
a word with you. all right?

192
00:13:44.920 --> 00:13:46.040
Just you and me.

193
00:13:47.240 --> 00:13:49.920
You won't be bullied. will you?
I'm starting to see that.

194
00:13:51.160 --> 00:13:52.616
It's admirable.

195
00:13:52.640 --> 00:13:55.360
But maybe political pragmatism
will work.

196
00:13:59.960 --> 00:14:02.256
The PM wants this deal.

197
00:14:02.280 --> 00:14:05.776
He says he's not gonna jeopardise
the future of 70 million people...

198
00:14:05.800 --> 00:14:07.256
DANNY SIGHS ...just because GCHQ

199
00:14:07.280 --> 00:14:09.216
can't get this thing under control.
Come on.

200
00:14:09.240 --> 00:14:12.280
But it's also about
something more important.

201
00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:16.136
His legacy.

202
00:14:16.160 --> 00:14:17.456
His place in the history books.

203
00:14:17.480 --> 00:14:19.376
Yeah. I know. I know.

204
00:14:19.400 --> 00:14:21.320
Political pragmatism. Danny.

205
00:14:24.480 --> 00:14:26.736
China is his big thing.

206
00:14:26.760 --> 00:14:28.320
It has been for a long time.

207
00:14:29.480 --> 00:14:31.896
When he was my junior at Trade.

208
00:14:31.920 --> 00:14:34.256
he was the one who pushed through
that nuclear deal.

209
00:14:34.280 --> 00:14:37.056
Now. he wants nothing less

210
00:14:37.080 --> 00:14:39.776
than resetting
China's relationship with the West.

211
00:14:39.800 --> 00:14:43.256
and you. me. even GCHQ.

212
00:14:43.280 --> 00:14:45.080
we are just a means to that end.

213
00:14:46.400 --> 00:14:47.600
And the worm?

214
00:14:51.040 --> 00:14:54.176
I've heard it's a potentially
nuclear-level threat.

215
00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:57.616
Wow. I'm flattered -
you're quoting me back to me.

216
00:14:57.640 --> 00:14:59.576
Can you just give me something?

217
00:14:59.600 --> 00:15:01.320
Are you any nearer to finding a fix?

218
00:15:02.360 --> 00:15:03.576
We're working on something -

219
00:15:03.600 --> 00:15:06.296
Roz Cavendish. myself.
the whole team together.

220
00:15:06.320 --> 00:15:08.536
OK. OK. that is good to hear.

221
00:15:08.560 --> 00:15:10.256
Right. I'm gonna go back in there

222
00:15:10.280 --> 00:15:13.496
and tell him that I hauled you over
the coals but you're nearly there.

223
00:15:13.520 --> 00:15:15.680
and that crucially. for him...

224
00:15:16.960 --> 00:15:19.240
we're not gonna rock China's boat.
Yes?

225
00:15:20.440 --> 00:15:21.816
Thank you.

226
00:15:21.840 --> 00:15:23.560
Political pragmatism. Danny.

227
00:15:25.200 --> 00:15:26.360
Now you owe me.

228
00:15:46.680 --> 00:15:47.816
Have you got a question.

229
00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:49.776
or are you just here
to see how it's done?

230
00:15:49.800 --> 00:15:51.656
How near? Near.

231
00:15:51.680 --> 00:15:53.360
Good. Do you have a minute?

232
00:15:59.480 --> 00:16:01.096
Guys. can we have the room. please?
Yeah.

233
00:16:01.120 --> 00:16:02.200
Thank you.

234
00:16:04.840 --> 00:16:07.136
DANNY CLEARS HIS THROAT Marston.

235
00:16:07.160 --> 00:16:10.176
What about him?
We're not really that close. Danny.

236
00:16:10.200 --> 00:16:12.776
Him and the Prime Minister -
what's the deal there?

237
00:16:12.800 --> 00:16:15.376
Like I said. we're not close.

238
00:16:15.400 --> 00:16:17.656
Marston was president
at the Board of Trade

239
00:16:17.680 --> 00:16:19.616
when Makinde was a junior there.

240
00:16:19.640 --> 00:16:22.936
then Makinde leapfrogged Marston
and everyone else

241
00:16:22.960 --> 00:16:24.240
and got the top job.

242
00:16:26.040 --> 00:16:28.376
Richard's... pragmatic.

243
00:16:28.400 --> 00:16:29.976
I always understood he was just

244
00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:32.216
hitching his waggon
to the greater star.

245
00:16:32.240 --> 00:16:35.000
Makinde's got more of
the common touch.

246
00:16:36.640 --> 00:16:39.696
And you're sure
there's no more to it than that?

247
00:16:39.720 --> 00:16:42.936
No. but I don't think about it
that much.

248
00:16:42.960 --> 00:16:44.800
Like I said - not close.

249
00:16:46.200 --> 00:16:48.216
And I've got a tar pit to build.

250
00:16:48.240 --> 00:16:49.480
OK. thank you.

251
00:16:53.480 --> 00:16:54.760
It's clear now...

252
00:16:56.520 --> 00:17:00.200
that our colleague. Calvin. has
been working for a hostile power.

253
00:17:02.280 --> 00:17:06.280
But this news
does not make Calvin a monster.

254
00:17:09.560 --> 00:17:13.200
He is a good friend and colleague.

255
00:17:14.360 --> 00:17:16.456
We don't know
what pressure he was under.

256
00:17:16.480 --> 00:17:18.280
what threats were made.

257
00:17:21.160 --> 00:17:24.856
We have to be dispassionate
in our judgment.

258
00:17:24.880 --> 00:17:27.920
and compassionate towards him...

259
00:17:30.160 --> 00:17:32.376
focus on ourselves...

260
00:17:32.400 --> 00:17:34.720
on our mission. on recovery...

261
00:17:36.560 --> 00:17:38.760
and don't let
the corrosion spread.

262
00:17:46.040 --> 00:17:47.896
QUIETLY: Thank you. team.

263
00:17:47.920 --> 00:17:50.120
They've already cleared
Calvin's desk. Barbara.

264
00:19:21.960 --> 00:19:25.800
VIDEO CALL RINGS

265
00:20:53.640 --> 00:20:57.536
We'll connect these virtual nodes
to the infected network.

266
00:20:57.560 --> 00:21:00.656
The nodes replicate the pattern
of the worm's first few moves.

267
00:21:00.680 --> 00:21:03.376
The worm thinks it's entering
a real server.

268
00:21:03.400 --> 00:21:04.776
It jumps inside.

269
00:21:04.800 --> 00:21:06.016
And then it loops?

270
00:21:06.040 --> 00:21:07.576
Exactly. It's trapped.

271
00:21:07.600 --> 00:21:09.376
And we can also have
a good look at it then.

272
00:21:09.400 --> 00:21:10.600
Excellent work.

273
00:21:41.440 --> 00:21:43.640
HE SIGHS

274
00:22:40.800 --> 00:22:43.696
And you need to
access these files why?

275
00:22:43.720 --> 00:22:46.936
{\an8}I'm concerned that there's
something underpinning

276
00:22:46.960 --> 00:22:48.536
{\an8}the Government's lack of support

277
00:22:48.560 --> 00:22:50.216
for our response to the worm attack

278
00:22:50.240 --> 00:22:53.296
and I think it dates back
to the China nuclear energy deal

279
00:22:53.320 --> 00:22:54.696
a few years ago.

280
00:22:54.720 --> 00:22:56.216
Marston and the Department of Trade

281
00:22:56.240 --> 00:22:58.816
were given a clean bill of health
at the inquiry.

282
00:22:58.840 --> 00:23:02.216
Makinde was Marston's
junior Trade Minister at the time.

283
00:23:02.240 --> 00:23:04.656
but he was never
investigated individually -

284
00:23:04.680 --> 00:23:06.816
the whole focus was on Marston.

285
00:23:06.840 --> 00:23:08.856
I searched
the National Security holdings

286
00:23:08.880 --> 00:23:11.360
and I found these recordings. sealed.

287
00:23:12.440 --> 00:23:15.016
MI5 saw fit to bug the negotiations.

288
00:23:15.040 --> 00:23:17.536
extracts from which
were redacted and sealed

289
00:23:17.560 --> 00:23:20.136
on the day Makinde
became Prime Minister.

290
00:23:20.160 --> 00:23:23.536
Look. firstly. you know material is
redacted for all sorts of reasons -

291
00:23:23.560 --> 00:23:26.416
an off joke about President Xi
or some such.

292
00:23:26.440 --> 00:23:29.016
Well. then why are they
in our holdings. sealed. then?

293
00:23:29.040 --> 00:23:31.856
Because. I imagine.
we did some translation.

294
00:23:31.880 --> 00:23:33.880
interpretation or security work
on them.

295
00:23:35.120 --> 00:23:36.520
It was before my time.

296
00:23:37.880 --> 00:23:39.056
But I can't...

297
00:23:39.080 --> 00:23:42.936
Danny. I know relations between you.
indeed. us.

298
00:23:42.960 --> 00:23:44.760
and the Government are strained...

299
00:23:45.800 --> 00:23:47.016
but you have no proof

300
00:23:47.040 --> 00:23:50.440
the Prime Minister is
in any way influenced by China.

301
00:23:52.160 --> 00:23:53.776
Open them yourself. then.

302
00:23:53.800 --> 00:23:55.056
Listen to them.

303
00:23:55.080 --> 00:23:56.680
Tell me there's nothing in them.

304
00:23:59.160 --> 00:24:03.800
If I were to open these files.
it would doubtless be flagged.

305
00:24:04.920 --> 00:24:07.360
{\an8}I mean. it could be seen to be
a declaration of war.

306
00:24:09.080 --> 00:24:12.760
We do security and technology.
never politics.

307
00:24:13.880 --> 00:24:16.200
That is our line in the sand.
is that clear?

308
00:24:18.760 --> 00:24:20.520
Yes. Of course.

309
00:24:27.000 --> 00:24:28.000
DOOR CLOSES

310
00:24:31.400 --> 00:24:32.720
HE SIGHS

311
00:24:34.400 --> 00:24:36.456
Are we nearly there? Minutes away.

312
00:24:36.480 --> 00:24:39.776
We're installing the tar pit into
all the gov. uk startup services.

313
00:24:39.800 --> 00:24:42.336
The tar pit launches
when we reboot the servers.

314
00:24:42.360 --> 00:24:44.376
It generates virtual IP addresses.

315
00:24:44.400 --> 00:24:47.296
The worm thinks they're real IPs
and propagates from one to the next.

316
00:24:47.320 --> 00:24:49.376
It's like a hall of mirrors.

317
00:24:49.400 --> 00:24:53.056
All that decoy data you added -
beautiful script.

318
00:24:53.080 --> 00:24:54.656
You worked in the field. right?

319
00:24:54.680 --> 00:24:56.536
GCO. tour of Afghan. Kandahar.

320
00:24:56.560 --> 00:24:59.216
This is very touching.
but we need to go live ASAP.

321
00:24:59.240 --> 00:25:01.736
We're ready. boss. All integrated.

322
00:25:01.760 --> 00:25:05.016
OK. Max. call heads of IT
at Trade and Immigration.

323
00:25:05.040 --> 00:25:06.976
tell them we're putting them
back online.

324
00:25:07.000 --> 00:25:09.576
Oh. and you might wanna
let Number 10 know as well.

325
00:25:09.600 --> 00:25:11.496
and the Foreign Secretary.

326
00:25:11.520 --> 00:25:12.776
Courtesy.

327
00:25:12.800 --> 00:25:14.480
Roz. when you're ready.

328
00:25:20.800 --> 00:25:22.000
Here we go.

329
00:25:38.200 --> 00:25:39.640
It's found our fake host.

330
00:25:47.160 --> 00:25:49.040
We've got it. It's trapped.

331
00:25:50.640 --> 00:25:51.760
Yes!

332
00:25:54.840 --> 00:25:57.496
Let's get Trade and Immigration
back online.

333
00:25:57.520 --> 00:25:58.840
Great work. everyone.

334
00:26:11.400 --> 00:26:12.880
Maybe you should come with me.

335
00:26:14.320 --> 00:26:16.040
Your friend's gonna get me a visa?

336
00:26:18.280 --> 00:26:19.400
I could ask.

337
00:26:20.400 --> 00:26:21.760
Give up my whole life?

338
00:26:25.920 --> 00:26:29.136
Maybe I like my home and my city.

339
00:26:29.160 --> 00:26:31.856
my family and my friends.

340
00:26:31.880 --> 00:26:34.096
Everyone always thinks
Chinese people

341
00:26:34.120 --> 00:26:37.056
are the way our government
wants us to be -

342
00:26:37.080 --> 00:26:41.240
no individuality.
hardworking. obedient.

343
00:26:42.280 --> 00:26:43.560
Try being Russian.

344
00:26:46.200 --> 00:26:47.280
When I was younger...

345
00:26:48.360 --> 00:26:51.040
all I wanted was to
run away from my family.

346
00:26:52.360 --> 00:26:54.600
I blamed them for being obedient.

347
00:26:55.640 --> 00:26:57.000
But now...

348
00:26:58.080 --> 00:27:01.176
Now I see
it's because they loved me.

349
00:27:01.200 --> 00:27:02.520
They wanted to protect me.

350
00:27:04.640 --> 00:27:07.536
And I'd be scared
to leave them behind.

351
00:27:07.560 --> 00:27:09.320
The MSS are already watching.

352
00:27:11.040 --> 00:27:12.960
Blind obedience is all they want.

353
00:27:14.200 --> 00:27:15.440
I can't live like that.

354
00:27:16.760 --> 00:27:18.640
PHONE CHIMES

355
00:27:24.240 --> 00:27:25.616
Ah!

356
00:27:25.640 --> 00:27:28.880
Ugh... SIREN WAILS.

357
00:27:31.320 --> 00:27:33.360
INDISTINCT SHOUTING

358
00:27:40.480 --> 00:27:41.720
Fuck.

359
00:28:17.520 --> 00:28:19.440
RADIO CHATTER

360
00:28:20.480 --> 00:28:21.760
Move. Russki!

361
00:28:25.480 --> 00:28:28.216
They told me to wait where I was.
So they can pick up your body?

362
00:28:28.240 --> 00:28:30.000
Only an idiot
would trust the English.

363
00:28:31.880 --> 00:28:32.896
Hey. What?

364
00:28:32.920 --> 00:28:34.496
Cage. In. What?!

365
00:28:34.520 --> 00:28:36.176
Now. What are you doing?

366
00:28:36.200 --> 00:28:37.976
Ordering a parcel delivery. Go!

367
00:28:38.000 --> 00:28:40.320
RATTLING

368
00:28:44.080 --> 00:28:45.200
APP CHIMES

369
00:28:49.280 --> 00:28:51.056
{\an8}Tell your friends
we need their help now.

370
00:28:51.080 --> 00:28:53.200
{\an8}not after some piss-assed
talks with CCP.

371
00:28:56.000 --> 00:28:58.776
All right. all right. the worm
has officially been contained.

372
00:28:58.800 --> 00:29:00.736
Government systems are back up
and running.

373
00:29:00.760 --> 00:29:02.736
Roz. Saara. Phil...
COMPUTER CHIMES.

374
00:29:02.760 --> 00:29:05.456
Lieutenant Williams in particular.
excellent work.

375
00:29:05.480 --> 00:29:07.016
Enjoy the moment.

376
00:29:07.040 --> 00:29:09.536
But containment is not a victory.

377
00:29:09.560 --> 00:29:11.936
We still need to know
what it's after...

378
00:29:11.960 --> 00:29:13.160
OK?

379
00:29:15.640 --> 00:29:17.136
Danny. Yeah?

380
00:29:17.160 --> 00:29:19.536
It's Vadim. on Discord.

381
00:29:19.560 --> 00:29:22.336
The safehouse where he's been hiding
has been raided.

382
00:29:22.360 --> 00:29:24.176
They're trapped in the building.

383
00:29:24.200 --> 00:29:25.696
We have to get him out.

384
00:29:25.720 --> 00:29:26.976
MI6?

385
00:29:27.000 --> 00:29:29.336
Well. we'd need
the Foreign Secretary's permission.

386
00:29:29.360 --> 00:29:30.936
And he'd need the PM's sign-off.

387
00:29:30.960 --> 00:29:33.056
And he's not going to do anything
to put his trade deal at risk.

388
00:29:33.080 --> 00:29:36.456
But we need that ciphertext.
It's the key we've been looking for.

389
00:29:36.480 --> 00:29:38.416
Now. we can't afford to wait for MI6.

390
00:29:38.440 --> 00:29:40.736
We've got to get him out ourselves.

391
00:29:40.760 --> 00:29:43.200
If you're not comfortable with that.
I understand.

392
00:29:53.560 --> 00:29:55.576
Williams. I'll need you
in the comms room with me.

393
00:29:55.600 --> 00:29:57.976
Saara. of course.
Max. you're watch officer.

394
00:29:58.000 --> 00:29:59.080
Yeah. go.

395
00:30:07.040 --> 00:30:08.056
OK. where are we at?

396
00:30:08.080 --> 00:30:10.000
Assembling the picture
on the ground.

397
00:30:11.480 --> 00:30:13.680
Yeah. make contact. Saara.
We need visuals.

398
00:30:16.280 --> 00:30:17.320
Here we go.

399
00:30:18.720 --> 00:30:20.976
Saara? Vadim. this is Danny Patrick.

400
00:30:21.000 --> 00:30:23.576
I'm with
Lieutenant Colonel Roz Cavendish.

401
00:30:23.600 --> 00:30:26.536
Now. we're gonna get you
out of there... Uh-huh.

402
00:30:26.560 --> 00:30:28.776
But we need that ciphertext.

403
00:30:28.800 --> 00:30:30.976
{\an8}How about he gives it to you
in person. Mister.

404
00:30:31.000 --> 00:30:32.816
when you get him to England?

405
00:30:32.840 --> 00:30:35.336
Like I said. we'll get you out.

406
00:30:35.360 --> 00:30:37.136
Over to you. Saara.

407
00:30:37.160 --> 00:30:39.016
Vadim? Yeah?

408
00:30:39.040 --> 00:30:40.776
What do we do. Saara?

409
00:30:40.800 --> 00:30:43.216
We're tracking you through
the phone -

410
00:30:43.240 --> 00:30:44.536
do not switch off.

411
00:30:44.560 --> 00:30:46.536
{\an8}There's a fire escape door
on the ground floor.

412
00:30:46.560 --> 00:30:47.616
There's an alley.

413
00:30:47.640 --> 00:30:49.576
I've texted a friend.
a delivery driver -

414
00:30:49.600 --> 00:30:50.936
is it clear for him?

415
00:30:50.960 --> 00:30:52.840
Checking.
WILLIAMS: I'm in the CCTV.

416
00:30:54.760 --> 00:30:55.880
Alleyway is clear.

417
00:30:57.480 --> 00:30:59.216
OK. we've got you. Vadim.

418
00:30:59.240 --> 00:31:02.056
If we can see Vadim and Hai.
so can the MSS.

419
00:31:02.080 --> 00:31:03.400
They'll be here soon.

420
00:31:08.360 --> 00:31:10.136
We'll introduce a frequency shift.

421
00:31:10.160 --> 00:31:12.256
We overload
the building's power system

422
00:31:12.280 --> 00:31:14.016
by pumping in a dirty signal -

423
00:31:14.040 --> 00:31:15.880
knocks out the cameras
and lighting.

424
00:31:17.640 --> 00:31:18.840
Police.

425
00:31:22.160 --> 00:31:23.600
CRASHING

426
00:31:26.440 --> 00:31:27.496
Roz here.

427
00:31:27.520 --> 00:31:31.216
When we pull the lights. keep still.
wait for them to pass.

428
00:31:31.240 --> 00:31:33.680
then run for your lives.
head to the harbour.

429
00:31:41.760 --> 00:31:44.080
OK. frequency really climbing now.

430
00:31:53.240 --> 00:31:54.976
Can it go faster?

431
00:31:55.000 --> 00:31:56.960
WHISPERS: Come on. come on. come on.

432
00:31:59.960 --> 00:32:01.400
DANNY: They're right on top of them.

433
00:32:13.840 --> 00:32:15.360
Nearly there.

434
00:32:17.680 --> 00:32:18.840
Right. here we go.

435
00:32:25.160 --> 00:32:26.400
{\an8}All right. it's happening.

436
00:32:29.800 --> 00:32:32.000
Good. CCTV's offline.

437
00:32:42.880 --> 00:32:44.160
Come on. Vadim.

438
00:33:01.920 --> 00:33:03.376
Come on.

439
00:33:03.400 --> 00:33:05.896
LOUD CRASHING

440
00:33:05.920 --> 00:33:07.376
Go. go. go. go. go. go!

441
00:33:07.400 --> 00:33:09.336
VADIM PANTS

442
00:33:09.360 --> 00:33:10.560
Run. Vadim.

443
00:33:13.360 --> 00:33:15.240
VADIM GRUNTS

444
00:33:19.120 --> 00:33:20.120
What's happened?

445
00:33:22.160 --> 00:33:23.456
We don't know. Saara.

446
00:33:23.480 --> 00:33:25.160
Shit! End the surge.

447
00:33:28.160 --> 00:33:29.480
We've done what we can.

448
00:33:36.080 --> 00:33:37.816
Has this been actioned?

449
00:33:37.840 --> 00:33:40.056
Yep. that's been done.

450
00:33:40.080 --> 00:33:41.440
Well... Barbara?

451
00:33:42.760 --> 00:33:44.080
Charlie.

452
00:33:51.440 --> 00:33:52.920
I've got some bad news.

453
00:33:55.040 --> 00:33:58.336
I wanted to tell you before the
rest of the department found out.

454
00:33:58.360 --> 00:34:00.600
but... it's Calvin.

455
00:34:01.760 --> 00:34:03.000
He's been found dead.

456
00:34:04.480 --> 00:34:05.560
What?

457
00:34:06.640 --> 00:34:08.360
In his cell. hanged.

458
00:34:09.600 --> 00:34:10.720
Hanged?

459
00:35:07.240 --> 00:35:09.160
PHONE LINE RINGS

460
00:35:14.200 --> 00:35:15.440
BUSY TONE

461
00:35:16.560 --> 00:35:17.640
Fuck!

462
00:35:28.880 --> 00:35:30.416
PHONE LINE RINGS

463
00:35:30.440 --> 00:35:32.696
VOICEMAIL: Your call cannot be taken
at the moment.

464
00:35:32.720 --> 00:35:34.640
Please leave a message
after the tone.

465
00:35:35.960 --> 00:35:37.040
Nicky...

466
00:35:56.160 --> 00:35:57.160
Fuck!

467
00:36:27.720 --> 00:36:30.040
Danny. Barbara had it sent up.

468
00:36:35.680 --> 00:36:37.560
Danny. come and see this.

469
00:36:39.360 --> 00:36:40.736
Do you need a minute?

470
00:36:40.760 --> 00:36:42.480
Er. no. I'm absolutely fine.

471
00:36:43.520 --> 00:36:46.320
They're alive.
but Hai's got a problem.

472
00:36:51.920 --> 00:36:53.896
Well done on getting yourself
out of that building.

473
00:36:53.920 --> 00:36:56.176
Where are you now?
Hai's friend. the delivery driver.

474
00:36:56.200 --> 00:36:57.816
took us here
in the back of his truck

475
00:36:57.840 --> 00:37:01.376
and gave us this phone.
but we can't stay here forever.

476
00:37:01.400 --> 00:37:03.416
Don't worry. we'll get you out.

477
00:37:03.440 --> 00:37:06.040
And if they can get Vadim out.
they can get you out too. Hai.

478
00:37:08.160 --> 00:37:09.480
Hai. what's the problem.

479
00:37:11.680 --> 00:37:13.216
She texted her sister...

480
00:37:13.240 --> 00:37:15.536
It doesn't matter - we got out.

481
00:37:15.560 --> 00:37:18.416
We can't sit around
talking about our problems.

482
00:37:18.440 --> 00:37:21.216
You need to get Vadim out of China.
Mister.

483
00:37:21.240 --> 00:37:22.760
Tell us when you can.

484
00:37:33.280 --> 00:37:34.280
What?

485
00:37:35.760 --> 00:37:36.960
What are you looking at?

486
00:37:38.800 --> 00:37:41.440
It's not your fault
your parents have been arrested.

487
00:37:46.320 --> 00:37:47.920
Hai. the CCP are vindictive...

488
00:37:49.080 --> 00:37:50.296
like Putin.

489
00:37:50.320 --> 00:37:52.576
But I am the cause of this
for my family.

490
00:37:52.600 --> 00:37:56.000
No. no. THEY are -
the CCP. not you.

491
00:37:57.800 --> 00:38:00.600
You heard him - he's going to
get both of us out of here.

492
00:38:04.640 --> 00:38:07.120
Maybe if they have me.
they will let them go free?

493
00:38:09.000 --> 00:38:10.680
We both know
it doesn't work like that.

494
00:38:51.120 --> 00:38:52.120
Back in the car.

495
00:38:53.240 --> 00:38:55.816
What the fuck. Mum? Back in - now.

496
00:38:55.840 --> 00:38:57.536
It's. um...

497
00:38:57.560 --> 00:38:59.896
Change of plans - you're spending
the weekend at your granny's.

498
00:38:59.920 --> 00:39:02.936
No. I've got a date.
Elliot. car - now!

499
00:39:02.960 --> 00:39:04.616
This is not an exercise.

500
00:39:04.640 --> 00:39:06.280
Go. Go!

501
00:39:30.840 --> 00:39:35.376
It smashed through our defences.
yours could be vulnerable too. but...

502
00:39:35.400 --> 00:39:39.976
whatever it's looking for.
it's connected to the ciphertext.

503
00:39:40.000 --> 00:39:42.136
I've known you for 15 years.
Michaela.

504
00:39:42.160 --> 00:39:44.456
I've never asked you
for a favour like this.

505
00:39:44.480 --> 00:39:45.840
I wouldn't waste your time.

506
00:39:47.040 --> 00:39:50.016
Dan. if this asset
is as hot as you say.

507
00:39:50.040 --> 00:39:52.456
I still don't get why
you don't extract him yourselves.

508
00:39:52.480 --> 00:39:55.960
Well. neither do I.
but I intend to look into it.

509
00:39:57.120 --> 00:39:59.840
In the meantime.
the clock is ticking.

510
00:40:02.400 --> 00:40:03.920
I'll run it by General Perez.

511
00:40:12.320 --> 00:40:13.440
HE SIGHS

512
00:41:17.720 --> 00:41:18.720
HE SLAPS THE DESK

513
00:41:23.160 --> 00:41:25.200
SHE SOBS

514
